from pathlib import Path
p=Path("_site/index.html")
s=p.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
if 'id="research-debates-2006"' not in s:
  marker='id="lifelock-debate"'
  ix=s.find(marker)
  if ix<0: raise SystemExit("Life Lock section missing")
  pos=s.rfind("<section",0,ix)
  new='''<section class="section recovered-story" id="research-debates-2006"><div class="wrap narrow"><div class="chapter-marker"><span class="chapter-index">2006</span><span class="chapter-line"></span><span>THE ARGUMENTS THAT TAUGHT US</span></div><h2>Finding the answer was only half the fight.</h2><p>I've been reading the old forum discussions again. In <strong>Gap Aura: Everything You Wanted to Know</strong>, people tried to understand how one lightning aura could threaten both low and high mana setups. They discussed Holy Shock, Lightning Mastery, carefully balanced damage ranges, and what one player described as a repeating pattern of four damage outcomes. Some people shared theories; others challenged them. Some parts were deliberately kept secret.</p><p>Jay wanted the knowledge discussed openly, but wouldn't release a character clone out of respect for <strong>Rich and Clan XxSiC</strong>. Another contributor shared most of the recipe while keeping its final attribute to himself. Those weren't abstract arguments about game balance. They were conversations about real work people had spent months doing.</p><p>The thread mentions <strong>Adeem and Rich</strong> as players whose characters were difficult to defeat, and even compares another proposed build to the <strong>Adeemsrevenge clone</strong>. Seeing their names in the middle of these old arguments brings the whole scene back.</p><p class="archive-links"><a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20071011/http://jayofteror.com/index.php?showtopic=9691" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read Gap Aura discussion ↗</a></p><div class="recovered-divider"></div><h3>The one-hit Stun discovery</h3><p>On December 17, 2006, Neounk_BoT posted the precise trigger: <strong>90% chance to cast level 10 Stun on attack and on hit</strong>. He warned that the looping hits could also kill the attacker through Thorns. Blackbird said he'd tested it, and Jay's response was to ask people to find its counter. Within hours others were talking about lowering Smite damage and surviving the reflected damage. One discovery became everybody else's new problem.</p><p class="archive-links"><a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20071011/http://jayofteror.com/index.php?showtopic=15079" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read original Stun thread ↗</a></p><div class="recovered-divider"></div><h3>Trying to kill the unkillable</h3><p>Another thread asked how to defeat Funki PI. Players tried Mind Blast, Psychic Hammer, and unusual summoned-monster counters. One suggested using zombies to make a WarGod clone gain experience and lose access to its equipment. Rich / WarBandit challenged that explanation, arguing the character's crucial mana was saved directly rather than supplied by its equipment, and pointed toward a Baal Crab mana-burn interaction instead. Nobody was taking a claim on faith. They argued, tested, and offered to prove it in a game.</p><p>Then I found a reply from <strong>PIB-Xenom666, September 20, 2006</strong>, describing an even stranger counter. He put a chance to summon a <strong>“sucker”</strong> monster on a charm, killed other monsters until one appeared, and let it attack the Funky PI character. This is the same kind of summoned-monster trick I remember working on. Finding it written down by somebody else, while these discussions were still happening, brought that memory right back.</p><p class="archive-links"><a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20071011/http://jayofteror.com/index.php?showtopic=10321" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read Funki PI counter discussion ↗</a></p></div></section>'''
  s=s[:pos]+new+s[pos:]
  p.write_text(s,encoding="utf-8")
css=Path("_site/overhaul.css")
c=css.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
add="""
#research-debates-2006 .recovered-divider{height:1px;background:rgba(210,179,120,.20);margin:35px 0}
#research-debates-2006 h3{color:#e0cba8;font-size:clamp(21px,2.5vw,28px);margin:12px 0}
"""
if '#research-debates-2006 .recovered-divider' not in c: css.write_text(c+"\n"+add,encoding="utf-8")
